  "canonical": {
    "channels": [],
    "description": "WebAuthn-shaped grammar: the attestation object, its statement formats, and the authenticator extension inputs — the shape a FIDO profile publishes. Reconstructed from the shape of those structures; no upstream text copied.",
    "extras": {
      "cddl": {
        "capability_limits": [
          {
            "construct": "cddl.control_bits",
            "count": 1,
            "detail": "`.bits` reads an integer as a bit set whose positions are named by a group. The canonical constraint vocabulary has no bit-set facet, so the member keeps its integer type and the named group is recorded in `cddl_control`; which bits are legal is not enforced.",
            "locations": [
              "authenticator-data-layout"
            ]
          },
          {
            "construct": "cddl.control_cbor",
            "count": 1,
            "detail": "`.cbor` and `.cborseq` say a byte string carries a *nested* CBOR encoding of another type. The canonical model has no embedded-encoding facet, so the member stays a byte string and the embedded type is recorded in `cddl_control` — the nesting is described, not modelled.",
            "locations": [
              "attested-credential-data"
            ]
          },
          {
            "construct": "cddl.open_map_entry",
            "count": 2,
            "detail": "A table entry (`* label => values`) alongside named members admits any number of further entries whose keys are not enumerable. The named members are carried and the table becomes one open-content member named `*`; a map whose *whole* body is a table is modelled exactly, as a canonical `MAP`.",
            "locations": [
              "cose-key",
              "extension-outputs"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "members": [
          "cddl/06-real-world-webauthn-shaped.cddl"
        ],
        "root_rule": "attestation-object",
        "root_type": "attestation-object"
      }
